  "result": "I fixed it: `--help` now lists each option's short name before its long one (`-v, --verbose` instead of `--verbose, -v`).\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/formatting.py:319`, `join_options` was sorting names longest-prefix-first. I removed `reverse=True`. Names with the same prefix length still appear in the order they were declared.\n- **Tests:** I added two regression tests at the end of `tests/test_formatting.py`. One checks `join_options` directly; the other runs `--help` on a real command and checks for `-v, --verbose`. No existing tests needed updating.\n- **Results:** the full suite passes (1908 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). On the first full run, one unrelated test, `test_file_atomics` in `tests/test_arguments.py`, failed with a Windows \"access denied\" error on a temp file. It passed when I ran it without my change, three more times with it, and in a second full run, so it looks like an intermittent Windows file-lock problem rather than something this change caused.\n\nI haven't committed anything; let me know if you want a commit or PR.",
